      "title": "Sheikh Hasina’s extradition possible via ‘well-structured’ process: India’s High Commissioner to Bangladesh",
      "link": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/sheikh-hasinas-extradition-possible-via-well-structured-process-indias-high-commissioner-to-bangladesh/article71540564.ece",
      "description": "When Sheikh Hasina sought refuge after the fall of her government, ‘India had hardly any choice,’ Dinesh Trivedi says",
      "source_name": "The Hindu National",
      "published": "2026-10-03T14:10:29"
    },
    {
      "title": "India cannot give deadline on Hasina's extradition to Bangladesh: envoy",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/india-cannot-give-deadline-on-hasina-s-extradition-to-bangladesh-envoy-126100300777_1.html",
      "description": "India cannot give any deadline for ousted Bangladesh prime minister Sheikh Hasina's return as her extradition request is under examination through a legal process, Indian High Commissioner in Bangladesh Dinesh Trivedi said on Saturday.\n\"Nobody can give you a timeframe (over Hasina's return),\" Trivedi said at a discussion organised by a private think tank in Dhaka, while responding to questions related to the repeated requests from Dhaka for Hasina's extradition to Bangladesh.\nHasina, 79, has been living in India after she fled Dhaka following the collapse of her government in August 2024 in the face of a massive anti-government agitation.\nIndia's external affairs ministry has maintained that the Bangladesh government's request for extraditing Hasina is being examined in line with established processes.\n\"Again and again, the government of India has replied to this that there is a process, and the process is legal, and it is well structured,\" Trivedi said on Saturday.\nHe also said .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-03T14:57:34"
    }
